$ rgit reword side -m 'not here'
[stderr]
fatal: <H4:7> is not in the current branch's first-parent history (`rgit log --first-parent` lists what can be reworded)
[exit 128]
$ rgit update-ref refs/remotes/origin/main HEAD~1
$ rgit reword HEAD~1 -m 'pushed already'
[stderr]
fatal: <H2:7> "second commit" is already pushed (origin/main has it); rewording it would make the branches diverge
hint: pass --force to reword it anyway (you'll need `rgit push --force` afterwards)
[exit 128]
$ rgit reword HEAD -m 'not pushed yet'
Reworded <H3:7> -> <H5:7> "not pushed yet".
(was "third commit"; `rgit undo` takes it back)
$ rgit reword HEAD~1 -m 'pushed, but forced' --force
Reworded <H2:7> -> <H6:7> "pushed, but forced", 1 later commit rewritten.
(was "second commit"; `rgit undo` takes it back)
